    "summary": "The remaining finding was another git branch rule (a leading hyphen). handoffBranchName now also refuses a name that starts with '-', and rather than keep finding rules one at a time the pure test now cross-checks the function against git itself: it generates 11 x 11 x 6 patterns from tricky pieces (empty, '-', '.', 'a.lock', '.h', 'a.', 'x..y', {slug}, {type}, '/', '.x') and for every pattern handoffBranchName accepts it runs 'git check-ref-format --branch <name>', which throws (failing the test) if git rejects the name, so an accepted name is always one git accepts; 'git check-ref-format' confirmed '-bad', 'foo.lock/x', 'a..b' and 'x/.h' invalid and the two default-style names valid. '-{id}' and '-x/{id}' are in the explicit refusal lists of both the pure and the park-plan tests. On scope: the diff touches gate.ts only to add the optional createIssue flag to teamContext (every existing caller is unchanged; parkPlan needs it so that planning a park can never create a tracker issue, which the previous round required) and the t4 pure test only because it tests handoffBranchName, which this round fixes again; park-offer.ts is untouched. Earlier fixes stand (branch validated before any tracker or git access, no-write assertions on the tracker, repo and run store). Pure, park-plan and park-offer tests pass; tsc clean.",
